// Lesson 01 effects — reveal, wipe, and mark acceptance.
//
// This is NOT a standalone script: it is appended to ser-estar-lesson.script
// and run as ONE Animation Script. A slide holds a single Animation Script
// whose Run replaces that script's previous footprint, so running the effects
// as a second, separate script would delete the lesson scene the base script
// created. Appending keeps scene and effects in one footprint: reruns replace
// everything without duplication, and one undo restores the prior output.
//
// The flow still needs two Runs: first the base lesson alone (so the table,
// sentence, title, AND the parked paw performers exist and the renderer has
// measured bounds), then the combined source (so effect Check samples the
// rendered scene and resolves the performer bindings).
//
// Demonstrates one of each effect, each swept by a paw asset performer
// (instances created by the base lesson, parked off-screen so only their
// sweep sprites show):
//
// - reveal on the conjugation table as a composite subtree (cell text is
//   ordinary renderable content; empty layout slots stay out), drawn by the
//   "paw with chalk" asset,
// - wipe on one example translation sentence (a single text node holding the
//   full sentence), wiped by the "paw with rag" asset,
// - mark on the lesson title as a temporary overlay, circled by the
//   "paw empty" asset.
//
// Performer bindings use `node("...")` by scene name on purpose: effect Check
// only accepts visuals that already exist in the scene as Asset Instances, so
// the snippet cannot reference the base script's `create` aliases directly —
// the base Run must create them first.
//
// Laser note for the mark: the renderer always centers the performer sprite
// on the mark pen point, so a shoot-from-a-distance look has to be baked into
// the "paw empty" image itself — put the beam tip at the image center with the
// paw body offset into transparent padding, and the on-screen paw will float
// at a distance while its tip touches the mark circle.
//
// Timing sits inside the base lesson so seeks stay meaningful: the mark draws
// while the title is shown, the table reveal runs once the table is fully
// filled (last cell fades in by 14.0, next examples start at 15.6), and the
// wipe runs after its example appears. The reveal carries an optional
// `sound:` SFX; the wipe and mark stay silent.
//
// Binding names are prefixed (`egrid`, ...) so they cannot collide with the
// base lesson's bindings when concatenated.
bind egrid = table("Grammar table")
bind esentence = node("ex1t")
bind etitle = node("Lesson title")
bind echalk = node("paw with chalk")
bind erag = node("paw with rag")
bind eempty = node("paw empty")
bind esfx = audio("Scratch")
mark(etitle, at: 1, over: 1, visual: eempty)
reveal(egrid, at: 14.5, over: 1, visual: echalk, sound: esfx)
wipe(esentence, at: 18, over: 1, visual: erag)
